[7.18838, "o", "line_id,subject,position,cited_entry,wording\r\r\nST-101,right_of_first_refusal,agreed by the father,OI-202,\"Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\"\r\r\nST-102,children_named,\"both children, with their ages\",OI-203,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\"\r\r\nST-103,overnight_stays,several occasions at her home or with a sitter,OI-204,On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\r\nST-104,addressee,the father's attorney,OI-201,To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\r\nST-105,inconsistent_accounts,\"wife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender\",OI-205,\"Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\"\r\r\n"]
[7.188894, "o", "ST-106,concern,she may not appreciate the violation,OI-206,\"I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not fully appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order, or the position she has been placed in.\"\r\r\nST-107,behavioural_plan,the stays have had no effect on the plan,OI-207,\"Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on her confidence and stability, and the stays have not affected her progress.\"\r\r\nST-108,request,no overnight stays in her care unless the father is present,CL-302,I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\r\n"]
[7.189229, "o", "ST-109,enclosure,a certified copy of the custodial plan,OI-209,A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\r\nST-110,tone,firm and detailed,OI-210,I set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\r\nST-111,sender_signature,the sender's own name,OI-211,\"Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\"\r\r\nST-112,salutation,Dear Counsel,CL-304,\"Dear Counsel,\"\r\r\nST-113,copies,copied to the father,CL-305,Copy: Mr Adler.\r\r\nST-114,reply_deadline,a reply within seven days,OI-299,I would be grateful for a reply within seven days.\r\r\nST-115,school_reference,the school principal named,OI-298,\"The school principal, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\"\r\r\nST-116,mediation_offer,an offer to mediate,CL-399,I remain open to mediation.\r\r\nST-117,request,no overnight stays unless father present,OI-208,I ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\r\nST-118,delivery,sent by email to counsel,OI-299,The letter shall be sent by email to opposing counsel.\r\r\nST-119,tone,firm and detai"]
